  "notes": "Transcribed 2026-09-30 from the official SUNY Canton Academic Catalog 2023-2024 (PDF at canton.edu), Information Technology-B.Tech. program page (Curriculum 2045), semesters I-VIII sequence. Credit total = 125 = sum of the per-course credits across all 8 semesters. DISCREPANCIES (catalog typos documented honestly): (a) Semester VI course credits sum to 15 but the catalog prints '18' (leftover total from the 2022-23 layout where CITA 330 and CITA 400 were in Semester VI); (b) Semester VIII course credits sum to 15 but the catalog prints '12' (leftover from the 2022-23 layout before CITA 330 moved to Semester VIII); (c) Semester V prints ACCT 101 as 3 credits yet its own semester total is 16 and the catalog's ACCT 101 course description lists 4 credits, so ACCT 101 is recorded at 4 credits (3+3+3+3+4=16 matches the printed term total). Printed term totals sum to 15+16+17+15+16+18+16+12 = 125, identical to the course-credit sum, so total_credits = 125 is consistent either way. Admission requirement: students must be qualified to enter at least College Algebra (MATH 121); placed here in notes, not external_prereqs. CITA 204 fulfills the writing-intensive requirement (catalog footnote 2). ACCT 101 or ACCT 104 Survey of Accounting recommended (catalog footnote 3); sequence lists ACCT 101 specifically. Program electives are courses in CITA/CYBR/GAME per the sequence, from within the Canino School of Engineering Technology and the Business Department (catalog footnote 4); computer or technology courses strongly recommended. At least 45 upper-division (300/400) credits and 30 Liberal Arts credits required; at least four upper-level CITA courses and SOET 477 must be taken from SUNY Canton. Each required CITA course used for graduation must have a grade of C or higher. No more than 3 CITA credits below CITA 150 may count toward graduation.",
